## Heading Styles

### H1 - Page Title
<h1 className="text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight">Main Page Heading</h1>

```tsx
<h1 className="text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight">Main Page Heading</h1>
```

### H2 - Section Title
<h2 className="text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Section Heading</h2>

```tsx
<h2 className="text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Section Heading</h2>
```

### H3 - Subsection Title
<h3 className="text-2xl font-semibold">Subsection Heading</h3>

```tsx
<h3 className="text-2xl font-semibold">Subsection Heading</h3>
```

### H4 - Component Title
<h4 className="text-xl font-medium">Component Heading</h4>

```tsx
<h4 className="text-xl font-medium">Component Heading</h4>
```

## Body Text Styles

### Large Body Text
<p className="text-lg leading-relaxed">
  Large body text for introductions and emphasis. This size is ideal for lead paragraphs and important content that needs extra visibility.
</p>

```tsx
<p className="text-lg leading-relaxed">...</p>
```

### Regular Body Text
<p className="text-base leading-normal">
  Regular body text for general content. This is the default size for most paragraphs and standard UI text. It balances readability with efficient use of space.
</p>

```tsx
<p className="text-base leading-normal">...</p>
```

### Small Body Text
<p className="text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
  Small text for secondary information, captions, and helper text. Use sparingly to maintain hierarchy.
</p>

```tsx
<p className="text-sm text-muted-foreground">...</p>
```

### Extra Small Text
<p className="text-xs text-muted-foreground">
  Extra small text for timestamps, metadata, and fine print.
</p>

```tsx
<p className="text-xs text-muted-foreground">...</p>
```

## Code Typography

### Inline Code
Regular text with <code className="px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded bg-muted text-sm font-mono">inline code</code> formatting.

```tsx
<code className="px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded bg-muted font-mono">const x = 1;</code>
```

### Code Blocks
```typescript
function greet(name: string): string {
  return `Hello, ${name}!`;
}
```

## Line Heights

We use semantic line-height values for optimal readability:

- `leading-none` (1) - For headings and compact text
- `leading-tight` (1.25) - For subheadings
- `leading-snug` (1.375) - For UI elements
- `leading-normal` (1.5) - Default for body text
- `leading-relaxed` (1.625) - For larger body text
- `leading-loose` (2) - For extremely readable text

## Letter Spacing

- `tracking-tighter` (-0.05em) - Very tight spacing
- `tracking-tight` (-0.025em) - Tight spacing for large headings
- `tracking-normal` (0em) - Default tracking
- `tracking-wide` (0.025em) - Wide spacing for small caps
- `tracking-wider` (0.05em) - Very wide spacing

## Text Colors

### Primary Text
<p className="text-foreground">Primary text color (--foreground)</p>

### Muted Text
<p className="text-muted-foreground">Muted text color for less important content</p>

### Destructive Text
<p className="text-destructive">Error or destructive action text</p>

### Primary Brand Text
<p className="text-primary">Primary brand color text</p>

## Tailwind Classes Quick Reference

```tsx
// Size
text-xs    // 0.75rem
text-sm    // 0.875rem
text-base  // 1rem
text-lg    // 1.125rem
text-xl    // 1.25rem
text-2xl   // 1.5rem
text-3xl   // 1.875rem
text-4xl   // 2.25rem

// Weight
font-light      // 300
font-normal     // 400
font-medium     // 500
font-semibold   // 600
font-bold       // 700

// Line Height
leading-none      // 1
leading-tight     // 1.25
leading-normal    // 1.5
leading-relaxed   // 1.625

// Color
text-foreground           // Primary text
text-muted-foreground     // Secondary text
text-primary              // Brand color
text-destructive          // Error color
```

## Accessibility Guidelines

1. **Minimum font size**: Use at least 14px (0.875rem) for body text
2. **Contrast**: Ensure 4.5:1 contrast ratio for normal text, 3:1 for large text (18px+)
3. **Line length**: Aim for 50-75 characters per line for optimal readability
4. **Line height**: Use at least 1.5 for body text
5. **Font weights**: Ensure sufficient weight differentiation between hierarchy levels

## Best Practices

- **Consistency**: Use the type scale consistently throughout your application
- **Hierarchy**: Establish clear visual hierarchy with font size, weight, and color
- **Readability**: Prioritize readability over aesthetics
- **Performance**: Font files are optimized and loaded via Google Fonts with `display: swap`
- **Responsiveness**: Consider using responsive font sizes for mobile devices

